. *
. * Clarke, Pailañir, Athey & Imbens (2023). sdid package.
. * Combines SCM-style unit weights with DiD-style time weights.
. * Estimate: ATT with placebo SEs (50 reps, seed 123), covariates projected.
. * NOTE: vce(bootstrap) requires ≥2 treated units and returns r(451) here.
. * vce(placebo) uses donor states as placebo units — correct for N_treated=1.
. 
. di as text "   Running sdid (placebo SE, 50 reps, covariate-adjusted)..."
   Running sdid (placebo SE, 50 reps, covariate-adjusted)...

. 
. * discard flushes any stale in-memory ado version that can cause r(198)
. capture discard

. 
. * ── Estimation and graph in ONE call ────────────────────────────────────────
. * MANUSCRIPT Fig. 10.7 - synthetic DiD, Georgia vs. synthetic control.
. *
. * The earlier r(198) was NOT a rendering failure.  -graph_export()- takes a
. * FILENAME PREFIX and a file type as two arguments, not a full path with an
. * extension; passing a complete filename returns r(198), which was
. * misdiagnosed for several revisions as sdid being unable to draw in do-file
. * context.  Verified interactively 15 Aug 2026: the call below produces
. * fig10_7_sdid_trends2018.png.
. *
. * sdid appends its own suffix to the prefix, so the exported file is
. * <prefix>trends<treatment year>.png -- here fig10_7_sdid_trends2018.png.
. * Estimation and graph are now a single call; -capture noisily- keeps the
. * export confirmation in the log.
. * SPECIFICATION (aligned with Section 10.6 of the manuscript, 15 Aug 2026).
. * This script previously ran sdid WITHOUT covariates, which returned
. * ATT = +0.0338 -- opposite in sign to the covariate-adjusted -0.01959 the
. * chapter reports and to the TWFE baseline.  Every other estimator in the
. * chapter conditions on $controls, so the unadjusted call was the outlier.
. * The call below matches the manuscript exactly: treat_sdid as the treatment
. * variable, seed(123), 50 placebo replications, and the four baseline
. * controls projected out.
. capture drop treat_sdid

. gen byte treat_sdid = did

. label var treat_sdid "Georgia x Post-2018 (SDID treatment indicator)"

. 
. capture noisily {
.     sdid lngenop fips fy treat_sdid, vce(placebo) seed(123) ///
>         covariates($controls, projected) ///
>         graph graph_export("$graphs_dir/fig10_7_sdid_", .png)
